A":"Careful is an adjective; the task asks for an adverb describing the action.","B":"Carefulness is a noun, not a manner adverb.","C":"Care is not the required manner adverb.","D":"**Carefully** tells us how they perform the action."}}},{"id":"9fc18dc9-ebf9-5640-a0c1-e11b2c5151af","topicSlug":"adverbs-position","level":"A2","prompt":"Keep the object beside the verb in this neutral sentence about the old portrait.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"They restored the old portrait carefully."},{"id":"B","text":"They restored carefully the old portrait."},{"id":"C","text":"They careful restored the old portrait."},{"id":"D","text":"They restored the old portrait carefulness."}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Keep **verb + object** together, then add the manner adverb.","explanation":"The direct object follows the verb, and **carefully** follows the object.","keywords":["manner-word-order"],"skill":"manner-word-order","contextKey":"adverbs-position-2","fingerprint":"b3d29d86b3778a7581f730d5765f21dfc9abfe9e06339d6abc41fb2a2f9ac4be","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adverbials"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Keep **verb + object** together, then add the manner adverb.","The direct object follows the verb, and **carefully** follows the object.","Choose **They restored the old portrait carefully.**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The direct object follows the verb, and **carefully** follows the object.","B":"The adverb separates the transitive verb from its object in an awkward neutral order.","C":"Careful is an adjective, not the adverb needed here.","D":"Carefulness is a noun and does not modify the action in this position."}}},{"id":"f83eb360-dbe8-56d9-a9a7-a1df9afb3240","topicSlug":"adverbs-position","level":"A2","prompt":"Choose neutral word order for a routine involving the garden fence.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"She measures usually the garden fence."},{"id":"B","text":"She measures the garden fence usuallys."},{"id":"C","text":"She usual measures the garden fence."},{"id":"D","text":"She usually measures the garden fence."}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Place **usually before the main lexical verb**, while keeping verb and object together.","explanation":"The frequency adverb **usually** normally precedes the lexical verb in neutral order.","keywords":["neutral-frequency"],"skill":"neutral-frequency","contextKey":"adverbs-position-3","fingerprint":"5b87ae8a3a1935e3a3d0e68561d3eefdab5215e58c3df72e75102c06d6eaac48","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adverbials"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Place **usually before the main lexical verb**, while keeping verb and object together.","The frequency adverb **usually** normally precedes the lexical verb in neutral order.","Choose **She usually measures the garden fence.**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This puts usually between the transitive verb and its object.","B":"Usually is an adverb and does not take an -s agreement ending.","C":"Usual is an adjective; this position requires the adverb usually.","D":"The frequency adverb **usually** normally precedes the lexical verb in neutral order."}}},{"id":"5475b549-2e76-5067-a15c-a5c8fdaa873c","topicSlug":"adverbs-position","level":"A2","prompt":"Use the adverb, not the adjective: “The assistant is ____ ready to measure the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"usuals"},{"id":"B","text":"usualness"},{"id":"C","text":"usually"},{"id":"D","text":"usual"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The blank modifies how often the assistant is ready, so it needs a **frequency adverb**.","explanation":"After be, **usually** gives the frequency of the state ready.