or a routine involving the travel leaflet.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"She translates usually the travel leaflet."},{"id":"B","text":"She translates the travel leaflet usuallys."},{"id":"C","text":"She usual translates the travel leaflet."},{"id":"D","text":"She usually translates the travel leaflet."}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Place **usually before the main lexical verb**, while keeping verb and object together.","explanation":"The frequency adverb **usually** normally precedes the lexical verb in neutral order.","keywords":["neutral-frequency"],"skill":"neutral-frequency","contextKey":"adverbs-position-4","fingerprint":"5c83957d9349b8702fd61b5a4541d8827b68345416c6b523bc71387345531d43","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adverbials"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Place **usually before the main lexical verb**, while keeping verb and object together.","The frequency adverb **usually** normally precedes the lexical verb in neutral order.","Choose **She usually translates the travel leaflet.**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This puts usually between the transitive verb and its object.","B":"Usually is an adverb and does not take an -s agreement ending.","C":"Usual is an adjective; this position requires the adverb usually.","D":"The frequency adverb **usually** normally precedes the lexical verb in neutral order."}}},{"id":"c8a55785-6da9-5636-ac4f-859d21d38baa","topicSlug":"adverbs-position","level":"A2","prompt":"Use the adverb, not the adjective: “The assistant is ____ ready to translate the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"usuals"},{"id":"B","text":"usualness"},{"id":"C","text":"usually"},{"id":"D","text":"usual"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The blank modifies how often the assistant is ready, so it needs a **frequency adverb**.","explanation":"After 